With all due respect,

523
00:22:06,310 --> 00:22:07,711
I'm the only member here who was

524
00:22:07,745 --> 00:22:09,246 in Mr. Ryerson's original Glee Club;

525
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,147 therefore, I should be getting the first solo.

526
00:22:11,182 --> 00:22:13,049
Say what?

527
00:22:13,084 --> 00:22:15,485
It's the first song; it sets the precedent for everything.

528
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:17,787
Rachel, Artie's gonna sing the first solo, period.

529
00:22:17,822 --> 00:22:19,502
You and everyone else are gonna have plenty

530
00:22:19,523 --> 00:22:22,092 of opportunities for a solo; we'll all take turns.

531
00:22:22,126 --> 00:22:24,127
In fact, I was thinking for sectionals, we would do

532
00:22:24,161 --> 00:22:26,930 a medley from Grease.
Who wants the Sandy part?

533
00:22:26,964 --> 00:22:28,832
Is this even a discussion right now?!

534
00:22:28,866 --> 00:22:30,834
I'm the only person in this room who can play Sandy!

535
00:22:30,868 --> 00:22:33,069
- Why? Because you're white?
- Okay, I wouldn't dream

536
00:22:33,104 --> 00:22:36,106 of being Mrs. Saigon or black Dorothy from the Wiz,

537
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,620 but if we want to be taken seriously as a glee club,

538
00:22:38,643 --> 00:22:40,176 then it can't be about color or disability or whatever.

539
00:22:40,211 --> 00:22:42,245
It has to be about who has the best voice.

540
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:44,281
Exactly. That would be me.

541
00:22:47,351 --> 00:22:48,418
Let's warm up.

542
00:22:48,452 --> 00:22:49,692
Brad.

543
00:23:04,502 --> 00:23:05,969
I thought you were finishing up out here?

544
00:23:06,003 --> 00:23:08,004
I-I was just taking a little break.

545
00:23:08,039 --> 00:23:09,399
You just left the vacuum cleaner on

546
00:23:09,407 --> 00:23:10,807 so that I would think you were cleaning

547
00:23:10,842 --> 00:23:12,442 while you were goofing off with the sheet music.

548
00:23:12,476 --> 00:23:15,278
There is a division of labor in this house, Will.

549
00:23:15,313 --> 00:23:16,813
You do the cooking and cleaning,

550
00:23:16,848 --> 00:23:18,815 and I will carry our children when we have them.

551
00:23:18,850 --> 00:23:20,517
Which might not be anytime soon

552
00:23:20,551 --> 00:23:22,485 because I'm sure all this extra free work you're doing

553
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:24,020 for the Glee Club is tiring you out

554
00:23:24,055 --> 00:23:25,789 and making your sperm stressed.

555
00:23:25,823 --> 00:23:27,190
You're right.

556
00:23:27,225 --> 00:23:29,192
I am stressed.

557
00:23:29,227 --> 00:23:32,028
And I'm sure my sperm's stressed, too.
Mm-hmm.

558
00:23:32,063 --> 00:23:34,130
The Glee Club is one day old, and there's already in-fighting.

559
00:23:34,165 --> 00:23:36,733
Which is kind of my fault,

560
00:23:36,767 --> 00:23:38,368 because I asked who wanted the first solo,

561
00:23:38,402 --> 00:23:40,337 and Rachel and Mercedes both raised their hands,

562
00:23:40,371 --> 00:23:41,838 and I don't want to disappoint either of them.

563
00:23:41,873 --> 00:23:43,874
Just give it to whichever one is the most pathetic.

564
00:23:43,908 --> 00:23:46,309
It's much harder to be jealous of someone when you think

565
00:23:46,344 --> 00:23:47,911 you're better than they are.

566
00:23:47,945 --> 00:23:49,813
Even if they get something that you want.

567
00:23:49,847 --> 00:23:51,414
I love it when you're all smart.

568
00:23:51,449 --> 00:23:53,016
Oh.

569
00:23:55,953 --> 00:23:58,421
I'm only gonna ask you this once,

570
00:23:58,456 --> 00:24:01,725 and then I promise I will never bring up the Glee Club again.

571
00:24:01,759 --> 00:24:04,060
Okay.

572
00:24:04,095 --> 00:24:06,229
Is it worth it?

573
00:24:06,264 --> 00:24:07,864
I mean, you know
I'm a little bit psychic.

574
00:24:07,899 --> 00:24:09,566
I have a bad feeling about this.

575
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:12,369
How could anything bad come out of a glee club?

576
00:24:12,403 --> 00:24:14,571
Because look how distracted you are by it already.

577
00:24:14,605 --> 00:24:17,374
What if you end up spending so much time with the glee kids

578
00:24:17,408 --> 00:24:19,376 that you start neglecting our time together?

579
00:24:19,410 --> 00:24:21,211
I don't want to become one of those ignored wives

580
00:24:21,245 --> 00:24:22,279 who has an affair.

581
00:24:22,313 --> 00:24:24,915
You are the love of my life.

582
00:24:24,949 --> 00:24:28,385
And nothing is ever gonna take you away from me.

583
00:24:32,557 --> 00:24:34,157
Good.

584
00:24:35,455 --> 00:24:37,589
Mr. Schuester, how's the search for our male lead going?

585
00:24:37,623 --> 00:24:40,392
I took the initiative of making a list of potential candidates

586
00:24:40,426 --> 00:24:41,893
- based on their yearbook photos.
- Um, thanks, Rachel.

587
00:24:41,928 --> 00:24:43,762
But I was actually headed to the locker room

588
00:24:43,796 --> 00:24:46,098
- to see if, uh, any of the football players signed up. - Great.

589
00:24:46,132 --> 00:24:47,532
I also made a list of all the reasons

590
00:24:47,567 --> 00:24:49,034 why I should be getting the first solo.

591
00:24:49,068 --> 00:24:50,402
I think it would make an important statement

592
00:24:50,436 --> 00:24:51,937 to the rest of the team if you told them

593
00:24:51,971 --> 00:24:54,451 right at the beginning that I'm the star.

594
00:24:55,241 --> 00:24:57,709
Oh, my God.

595
00:24:57,744 --> 00:24:59,077
A-Are you okay?

596
00:25:01,247 --> 00:25:03,215
I told you.

597
00:25:03,249 --> 00:25:05,417
Everyone hates me.

598
00:25:07,253 --> 00:25:08,820
Everybody up!

599
00:25:08,855 --> 00:25:10,622
We're moving to the auditorium.

600
00:25:10,657 --> 00:25:11,990
Alcoholics Anonymous has the auditorium.

601
00:25:12,025 --> 00:25:13,291
Not anymore.

602
00:25:13,326 --> 00:25:15,060
Principal Figgins believes in us so much,

603
00:25:15,094 --> 00:25:16,294 he's giving it to us.

604
00:25:16,329 --> 00:25:18,096
For a while.

605
00:25:18,131 --> 00:25:20,966
Let's go. And grab a copy of
"You're the One That I Want."

606
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,467
Hold up, who gets to sing the Sandy part?

607
00:25:22,502 --> 00:25:24,036
Rachel.

608
00:25:25,104 --> 00:25:26,672
Are you serious?

609
00:25:26,706 --> 00:25:29,107
I can blow the roof off that auditorium.

610
00:25:29,142 --> 00:25:30,742
Her little bitty Jewish voice won't make it

611
00:25:30,777 --> 00:25:32,511
- past the third row.
- Racist!

612
00:25:32,545 --> 00:25:34,946
And untrue. I can belt just as good as you, better even.

613
00:25:34,981 --> 00:25:36,948
Oh, really?
Well, let's prove it.

614
00:25:36,983 --> 00:25:39,484
Let's have a sing-off right here, right now.

615
00:25:39,519 --> 00:25:41,253
We're not having a sing-off!

616
00:25:41,287 --> 00:25:43,255
Although that's not a bad idea for a future exercise.

617
00:25:43,289 --> 00:25:45,357
Rachel has this solo.

618
00:25:45,391 --> 00:25:46,658
Like I said, you'll all take turns.

619
00:25:46,693 --> 00:25:48,627
Except the white girl goes first.

620
00:25:48,661 --> 00:25:50,696
The white girl always goes first.

621
00:25:58,204 --> 00:26:00,205
Hey.

622
00:26:03,343 --> 00:26:05,344
I didn't get the solo.

623
00:26:07,347 --> 00:26:11,717
I lost it to that demented little Beanie Baby.

624
00:26:11,751 --> 00:26:15,187
Mr. Schuester is never gonna give me a solo.

625
00:26:15,221 --> 00:26:17,389
It's a waste of time;
I'm gonna quit.

626
00:26:17,423 --> 00:26:20,726
Nobody in there is gonna see me the way that I see myself.

627
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:22,728
Mercedes.

628
00:26:22,762 --> 00:26:24,029
You are so young.

629
00:26:24,063 --> 00:26:26,331
Glee Club just started.

630
00:26:26,333 --> 00:26:28,467
Who knows what your future holds?

631
00:26:28,501 --> 00:26:30,969
Mercedes,

632
00:26:31,004 --> 00:26:34,206 you are a star.

633
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,208
But part of the responsibility

634
00:26:36,242 --> 00:26:38,176 that goes along with being a star

635
00:26:38,211 --> 00:26:41,246 is learning to share the spotlight.

636
00:26:41,281 --> 00:26:45,150
Maybe she's gonna get the solos

637
00:26:45,184 --> 00:26:47,486 because she needs it more than you do right now.

638
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:51,189
Truth is, Mercedes, Rachel will make you better.

639
00:26:51,224 --> 00:26:53,425
Her drive and ambition

640
00:26:53,459 --> 00:26:56,261 will help you raise your expectations of yourself,

641
00:26:56,296 --> 00:26:58,730 and you can use that to become great.

642
00:26:58,765 --> 00:27:00,732
And I have a feeling

643
00:27:00,767 --> 00:27:02,868 you two are gonna become great friends.

644
00:27:05,972 --> 00:27:08,440
Stars have a way of finding each other.

645
00:27:08,474 --> 00:27:10,309
Okay, come here.

646
00:27:14,314 --> 00:27:15,547
There you go, Sue.

647
00:27:15,581 --> 00:27:16,949
Some principals would say

648
00:27:16,983 --> 00:27:20,052 that importing a rare silk trampoline mat

649
00:27:20,086 --> 00:27:23,622 from China is an extravagance, but not this principal.

650
00:27:23,656 --> 00:27:26,858
The Cheerios! Are McKinley
High's number one priority.

651
00:27:26,893 --> 00:27:29,094
Oh, thank you so much,
Principal Figgins.

652
00:27:29,128 --> 00:27:30,762
I could have never led my Cheerios!

653
00:27:30,797 --> 00:27:34,399
To a record five consecutive national championships

654
00:27:34,434 --> 00:27:36,301 without you.

655
00:27:36,336 --> 00:27:38,303
Actually, I could have done it very easily without you.

656
00:27:38,338 --> 00:27:40,619
Oh, uh, and that reminds me.
I have a question for you.

657
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:42,040
Hmm?

658
00:27:42,075 --> 00:27:43,909
What exactly is going on with Will Schuester

659
00:27:43,943 --> 00:27:45,377 taking over the show choir?

660
00:27:45,411 --> 00:27:47,212
The Glee Club?

661
00:27:47,246 --> 00:27:49,915
Why, Sue, that's nothing but a trifling.

662
00:27:49,949 --> 00:27:51,917
Well, I just want to be clear that the star performers

663
00:27:51,951 --> 00:27:53,919 at this high school are my Cheerios!,

664
00:27:53,953 --> 00:27:55,821 and I should hope it remains that way.

665
00:27:55,855 --> 00:27:57,456
Oh, Sue, don't worry.

666
00:27:57,490 --> 00:28:00,926
You are my star.
You are on Fox Sports Net.

667
00:28:00,960 --> 00:28:02,894
- Yes. - And besides, show choir won't last.

668
00:28:02,929 --> 00:28:06,598
Will only has five students, one of them a cripple.

669
00:28:06,633 --> 00:28:08,767
And children these days aren't interested

670
00:28:08,801 --> 00:28:11,136 in singing to each other.

671
00:28:11,170 --> 00:28:14,239
They're too busy with their Friendster and Myspace

672
00:28:14,274 --> 00:28:15,741 and Blockbuster Video.

673
00:28:15,775 --> 00:28:17,676
These are things that are here to stay.

674
00:28:17,710 --> 00:28:19,411
Well, I don't know.

675
00:28:19,445 --> 00:28:23,248
I have a bad feeling about this Glee Club.

676
00:28:31,624 --> 00:28:33,125
Come on, go!

677
00:28:33,159 --> 00:28:34,593
Okay, come on.

678
00:28:34,627 --> 00:28:36,495
Traveling.

679
00:28:36,529 --> 00:28:38,931
Hey!

680
00:28:38,965 --> 00:28:40,933
Hey, you know, because we're best friends,

681
00:28:40,967 --> 00:28:43,001
I want to ask you something frankly.
Sure.

682
00:28:43,036 --> 00:28:44,436
Wait, I-I'm your best friend?

683
00:28:44,470 --> 00:28:46,638
I-I know nothing about you.
We hardly even talk.

684
00:28:46,673 --> 00:28:48,440
We just play basketball once a week.

685
00:28:48,474 --> 00:28:50,208
Yeah, like I said, best friends.

686
00:28:51,477 --> 00:28:53,278
What are your...
Thank you.

687
00:28:53,313 --> 00:28:55,280
What are your intentions with this Glee Club?

688
00:28:55,315 --> 00:28:56,481
Intentions?
I don't know.

689
00:28:56,516 --> 00:28:58,150
I guess we'll have to find out.

690
00:28:58,184 --> 00:28:59,551
I don't know, I just...

691
00:28:59,586 --> 00:29:01,553
I look around this school,
I see all these kids

692
00:29:01,588 --> 00:29:02,988 who don't have the arts in their lives,

693
00:29:03,022 --> 00:29:04,990 and I want them to have what I had...

694
00:29:05,024 --> 00:29:07,392
A place where they can go to experience the joy of music.

695
00:29:07,427 --> 00:29:09,161
Yeah, well, they already have that, William.

696
00:29:09,195 --> 00:29:11,396
It's called the iPod.
I don't know, being a part

697
00:29:11,431 --> 00:29:13,465 of Glee Club was the best thing that ever happened to me.

698
00:29:13,499 --> 00:29:15,400
Now you're a high school
Spanish teacher.

699
00:29:16,703 --> 00:29:18,470
Will, the students at this school

700
00:29:18,504 --> 00:29:19,905 aren't going to become performers.

701
00:29:19,939 --> 00:29:21,240
They're not gonna become professional singers

702
00:29:21,274 --> 00:29:22,708 or dancers or actors.

703
00:29:22,742 --> 00:29:24,643
They'll be fry cooks and auto mechanics.

704
00:29:24,677 --> 00:29:27,479
And it's really unfair of you to suggest anything otherwise.

705
00:29:27,513 --> 00:29:31,250
Fostering unrealistic dreams in these kids will accomplish

706
00:29:31,284 --> 00:29:33,018 absolutely nothing but to make their lives

707
00:29:33,052 --> 00:29:36,321 that much more dark and depressing.

708
00:29:36,356 --> 00:29:39,191
I'm sorry, Sue.
I just disagree.

709
00:29:39,225 --> 00:29:41,159
I mean, the arts are important.

710
00:29:41,194 --> 00:29:43,495
Certainly more important than cheerleading.

711
00:29:43,530 --> 00:29:44,897
How dare you.

712
00:29:44,931 --> 00:29:46,565
And I think, with a little hard work,

713
00:29:46,599 --> 00:29:48,700 this Glee Club could really accomplish something.

714
00:29:48,735 --> 00:29:50,736
I got Finn Hudson to sign up,

715
00:29:50,770 --> 00:29:53,005 and he's the captain of the football team, so...

716
00:29:53,039 --> 00:29:54,706 who knows what our future could hold?

717
00:29:54,741 --> 00:29:57,376
I'm gonna give you an ultimatum, William.

718
00:29:57,410 --> 00:29:58,911
You either drop this Glee Club,

719
00:29:58,945 --> 00:30:01,213 or you and I will cease to be friends.

720
00:30:01,247 --> 00:30:02,807
What?

721
00:30:04,317 --> 00:30:05,717
Are you serious?

722
00:30:05,752 --> 00:30:07,185
You do not want to make

723
00:30:07,220 --> 00:30:09,588 an enemy out of Sue Sylvester.

724
00:30:09,622 --> 00:30:11,456
You don't want to do that.

725
00:30:18,164 --> 00:30:19,965
Sorry, Sue.

726
00:30:20,567 --> 00:30:22,634
No deal.

727
00:30:23,670 --> 00:30:25,671
♪ ♪

728
00:30:33,169 --> 00:30:35,470
The sun is not the biggest nor the brightest star in the sky.

729
00:30:35,504 --> 00:30:37,105
It's just the closest.

730
00:30:37,139 --> 00:30:39,374
There are bigger, brighter, better stars.

731
00:30:39,408 --> 00:30:41,042
That's what I am.

732
00:30:41,076 --> 00:30:44,012
I will be the biggest star of them all.

733
00:30:46,282 --> 00:30:49,117
Myspace is pretty much the greatest invention ever.

734
00:30:49,151 --> 00:30:52,053
It democratizes performance and lets anyone express themself

735
00:30:52,087 --> 00:30:54,789 to a wide audience from the comfort of their own home.

736
00:30:54,824 --> 00:30:57,759
That's why I invested all of my Bat Mitzvah money

737
00:30:57,793 --> 00:31:00,128 in the company.
Unfortunately, the Internet

738
00:31:00,162 --> 00:31:02,664 has also created the democratization of criticism.

739
00:31:02,698 --> 00:31:04,299
Now people can anonymously say things to me

740
00:31:04,333 --> 00:31:05,967 that they would never have the guts

741
00:31:06,001 --> 00:31:07,635 to say to my face.

742
00:31:07,670 --> 00:31:09,737
I am proud to say that I have grown numb

743
00:31:09,772 --> 00:31:11,972 to the cruelty, but none of it is going to happen

744
00:31:11,974 --> 00:31:14,943 if there's no Glee Club.
Rumor has it that Mr. Shue's

745
00:31:14,977 --> 00:31:17,412 horrible wife told him last night that she's with child.

746
00:31:17,446 --> 00:31:19,514
Time's are tough, and he's probably gonna leave us

747
00:31:19,548 --> 00:31:20,949 for a high-paying job.

748
00:31:20,983 --> 00:31:22,517
That's the inciting incident.

749
00:31:22,551 --> 00:31:24,586
Glee Club is the cosmic explosion that will

750
00:31:24,620 --> 00:31:27,155 propel the hot balloon of light and gas

751
00:31:27,189 --> 00:31:28,990 that is my stardom towards Earth...

752
00:31:29,024 --> 00:31:31,125
Specifically Midtown...
And without Will Schuester,

753
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,694 there's no Glee Club.

754
00:31:32,728 --> 00:31:34,688
There's no convincing him to change.

755
00:31:34,697 --> 00:31:37,632
If I want him to give up on this stupid accounting thing,

756
00:31:37,666 --> 00:31:40,201
I have to go talk directly to his boss.

757
00:31:40,236 --> 00:31:43,304
I am very aware that it is the job off the assistant manager

758
00:31:43,339 --> 00:31:46,541 to stock the novelty sheets,
Howard, but I am pregnant,

759
00:31:46,575 --> 00:31:49,043 and my doctor says I need to take it easy.

760
00:31:49,078 --> 00:31:51,045
- Are you on bed rest?
- Oh, not officially,

761
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:52,547 but I'm sure I will be soon enough.

762
00:31:52,581 --> 00:31:54,341
And even sooner, if you keep stressing me out

763
00:31:54,350 --> 00:31:56,310 by complaining that you can't do my job right now.

764
00:31:56,318 --> 00:31:58,219
No, no, no, I-I'm sorry.

765
00:31:58,254 --> 00:32:01,689
I'll-I'll just give up sleeping for a while to get it all done.

766
00:32:03,225 --> 00:32:05,059
Mrs. Schuester,
I'm Rachel Berry.

767
00:32:05,094 --> 00:32:06,461
I'm one of your husband's students,

768
00:32:06,495 --> 00:32:07,695
Glee Club specifically.

769
00:32:07,730 --> 00:32:10,465
- I'm working.
- First of all,

770
00:32:10,499 --> 00:32:12,233
I just wanted to congratulate you on your new addition.

771
00:32:12,268 --> 00:32:14,035
I can tell that you already have the pregnancy glow.

772
00:32:14,069 --> 00:32:15,904
Oh. Thank you.

773
00:32:15,938 --> 00:32:17,806
Second of all, I just wanted to ask you to reconsider guilting

774
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:20,542 your husband into quitting his job and becoming an accountant.

775
00:32:20,576 --> 00:32:23,311
Here's what I've learned in the years since I left high school.

776
00:32:23,345 --> 00:32:25,413
There's who you are, and there's who you think you are.

777
00:32:25,448 --> 00:32:27,715
